// LingOS — minimal aarch64 (Raspberry Pi) kernel entry point.
// Same ling_kernel_* intrinsic names as the x86_64 target; ling-kernel routes
// them to the PL011 UART instead of VGA/COM1 underneath.
bind start = do {
    ling_kernel_init()
    // Idle loop with a live on-screen uptime clock (polls the generic timer;
    // proof-of-life on Pi 5, which has no serial and no timer IRQs yet). It
    // prints the boot lines itself, then never returns. (The boot messages are
    // kernel-side because a do-block whose final expression is a plain call —
    // not asm! — drops the preceding intrinsic calls under the current AOT.)
    ling_kernel_rpi_idle()
}
